  "term": "hyperexcitability",
  "definition": "Hyperexcitability is a state in which neurons or neural networks are unusually prone to activation, making excessive brain activity more likely, as in seizure activity. In the supplied source, it is described as arising not only from the excitability of individual neurons but also from synaptic and network-level changes that increase overall responsiveness.",
